---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="about"
  description="About Cristian Gonzales: senior engineer at Microsoft, deep learning enthusiast, and builder of side projects."
>
  <header class="page-header">
    <p class="eyebrow">about / cristian's scratchpad</p>
    <h1>about</h1>
  </header>

  <article class="about-page">
    <p class="about-text">
      Cristian is currently a senior engineer at Microsoft, working on Office's
      <a
        href="https://www.nvidia.com/en-us/glossary/data-flywheel/"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Data Flywheel</a
      >
      efforts. Previously at Microsoft, he worked on a framework evaluating <a
        href="https://techcommunity.microsoft.com/blog/excelblog/building-agent-mode-in-excel/4457320"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Excel Agent Mode</a
      >, was a key contributor in helping bring <a
        href="https://loop.cloud.microsoft/learn"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Loop</a
      > to life at its inception, and also made contributions to code that <a
        href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/openspecs/office_protocols/ms-wopi/0f0bf842-6353-49ed-91c0-c9d672f21200"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">powers the way Office on the web talks to storage hosts</a
      >: think SharePoint, Dropbox. Before Microsoft, he had a brief stint at <a
        href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SoFi"
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener">Social Finance</a
      >, and also worked in the defense industry, working on both software and
      infrastructure!
    </p>

    <p class="about-text">
      You can catch him working on AI-centric passion projects with most of his
      free time, but when he's not in The Matrix, he occasionally enjoys going
      to country dance halls and being really bad at dancing, going to concerts
      and head banging, bingeing on true crime and reality TV with his
      girlfriend, and tending to his orange tabby cat (she is fat and orange,
      and her name is Maisie).
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
